# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Why `eol=lf` and not just `text=auto`: without it, a Windows checkout gets
# CRLF working-tree files while the repo stores LF, so `git status` reports ~200
# files as permanently modified. That stat-dirt blocked merges and rebases, had
# to be stashed before every integration, and — once Biome 2.5.5 started
# checking line endings — turned `bun run verify` red on a clean checkout.
#
# LF in the working tree is safe for this project: it is Bun/TypeScript, the
# shell scripts require LF anyway, and PowerShell 5.1+ reads LF fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these, line-ending translation corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.gz binary
*.wasm binary
*.zip binary
*.app binary
*.exe binary
*.db binary
*.snapshot binary
